        <body>
            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0476" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.61331/187: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sokobin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-07T14:00:00+08:00">December 7, 1939—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 7—9:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>221. Universal Leaf Tobacco Company will sign agreement tomorrow morning with the
                    Japanese military mission covering rights of purchase of 1,600,000 pounds of
                    leaf tobacco at five places on the railway, including Tsingtao, under conditions
                    along the lines of those outlined in my telegram 212, November 13, 11 a.m., but
                    with more liberal construction and concessions and with clause which will enable
                    company to purchase beyond the instant allotment if the size of the crop
                    permits.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping, Shanghai. Tokyo informed by telegram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sokobin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
